# Standard library

## Packages

GX code is organized in packages. Every file starts with a `package` clause: the lessons use the package `main`.

The `import` statement gives access to other packages, like the packages of the GX standard library. Names from an imported package are prefixed with the package name, as in `math.Sqrt`. Like in Go, a package only exports names starting with a capital letter.

Functions of the `math` package operate element-wise on arrays of any shape.

Several packages can be imported at once:

```
import (
    "math"
    "num"
)
```

